# A .bat with bare LF line endings is not a portable batch file: cmd.exe seeks
# through the file to resolve `goto`, and where that seek lands depends on the
# byte offsets, so a label the file plainly contains is reported missing --
# "The system cannot find the batch label specified" -- while the parts of the
# same file that do not jump run fine.  It therefore fails per-label, not
# per-file, which is why it reads as "this launcher is broken today".
#
# Git is the thing most likely to reintroduce it: whoever clones next may have
# core.autocrlf=input, and the experiment machine gets its code by pull.  So
# the checkout rule is stated here rather than left to each machine's config.
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Verilog constraints and sources are read by Vivado on Windows only.
*.xdc text eol=crlf
